{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/110293-true-fae-questions","id":110293,"title":"True fae questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-10T14:29:47-07:00","id":110293,"title":"True fae questions","content":"Can a changeling or some other supernatural kill a true fae? if yes, how?<br /> <br /> Are all changelings raped or otherwise mistreated?<br /> <br /> i read that fae are scared of mages, why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2331-rallen12","name":"Rallen12","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T14:51:03-07:00","id":110313,"title":"","content":"In order:<br /> <br /> 1) Yes, it is possible for a changeling to kill a True Fae. They do have stats, after all, and in particular Health, so they can absolutely be killed. Possibility is not the same thing as certainty, though. True Fae are very powerful, and killing one for good will take a freehold a whole lot of planning, teamwork, and luck.<br /> <br /> 2) All Changelings are abducted and held against their will, usually for quite a long time. They are also generally either pressed into servitude or tormented in some way. Which isn't to say that all Durances are unending hell - the Fairest in particular usually had some pleasurable element to theirs. But all PC Changelings were unhappy enough with their inprisonment to escape. (Unless someone is playing a privateer.)<br /> <br /> 3) Mages are powerful, versatile, and they like poking into secrets. Changelings like holding on to their secrets, and they like not being turned into flowerpots. They had quite enough of that in Arcadia, thank you very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2449-one-tin-soldier","name":"One Tin Soldier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2449_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T14:53:11-07:00","id":110318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rallen12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/110293-true-fae-questions#post110293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a changeling or some other supernatural kill a true fae? if yes, how?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, but you usually have to do it several times to make it stick. Most Faeries won't expose all of themselves at once precisely to stop themselves being killed.<br /> <br /> Just wait until the guy you remember as your Keeper is on Earth and fill him full of iron. It's the safest way, also you'll probably think you got all of it and the rest of it probably won't bother you again. You got the part of it that cared about you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rallen12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/110293-true-fae-questions#post110293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are all changelings raped or otherwise mistreated?</div> </div> </div> </div> No and no. But mistreatment is far more common than being treated kindly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rallen12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/110293-true-fae-questions#post110293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i read that fae are scared of mages, why?</div> </div> </div> </div>True Fae are not scared of Mages, and in fact frequently get the better of Archmages. Changelings are generally paranoid about everything.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T15:26:04-07:00","id":110337,"title":"","content":"<br /> #1) Probably, but it is hard to know for sure. Simply stabbing them often does not kill them...except when it does. It depends on the state of being of the Gentry and the Actor it is using. Thinking of a Gentry as a guy standing before you is not accurate exactly...except when it is.<br /> <br /> #2) Most Changelings are mistreated, but the only thing true of all Changelings is they are taken and came back. Some are raped, some not, some were even treated well. Depends on the Keeper, and what the Changeling's role was.<br /> <br /> #3) The Gentry are not afraid of Mages, or anything else except each other. Indeed, Mage magic may not even work properly in their realms, there is a template for Mages who entered the Hedge and became...things of the Hedge. Changelings tend to be a bit paranoid of anyone, and this includes Mages. They have no special fear of them though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T21:06:20-07:00","id":110570,"title":"","content":"1: This is more complicated a question than it sounds, as a True Fae might, at any given moment, exist as more than one person, place, thing, or group of the above. That said, each individual component of a True Fae will be vulnerable in some way (though likely incredibly tough and difficult to actually take out of play), and if someone were able to kill, destroy, defile, or otherwise render annihilated every piece of a Fae, that Fae would be well and truly dead. <br /> <br /> 2: Many were mistreated. A number were raped. Neither proportion is 100%, however. The main problem with the way the True Fae treat their kidnappees. is that it's inhuman and unhealthy. Even being doted on by a Keeper who styles herself as a loving mother-figure is likely to be a smothering, emotionally destructive experience. The Fae have literally no concept of other people as entities with feelings or needs that matter, and are *incapable* of forming such a concept. This, combined with the fact that emotions and personalities can be put on and taken off like well-worn hats, means that even the most pleasant Keeper can easily lead to a Durance of horrible uncertainty and empty pleasures. The happiness a human (or nascent Changeling) can find in Faerie is the same happiness a junkie finds at the point of his needle.<br /> <br /> 3: I'm Charlie Changeling. I've been kidnapped to the alien and eldritch realm of Arcadia, twisted by an all-powerful godlike being, and managed to escape. For the most part, I and those like me just want to avoid notice (which could draw the True Fae) and stay the crap away from Arcadia. But here comes Mickey Mage, a human with all-powerful, godlike powers. If he learns about me, he'll want to put me in the spotlight and under a microscope, learning all about what happened to me and opening painful memories in the process. He gained *his* powers by willingly visiting an alien and eldritch realm - possibly even one named Arcadia - and will likely do anything in his possible to get back... including forcing me to come along as a guide. So, in one person we have a dreadful reminder of the past, a terrible threat in the present, *and* a potential future catastrophe rolled into one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-13T12:02:01-07:00","id":112160,"title":"","content":"1-if found on earth cold iron usually does the trick, sure it might take a dozen or so of your buddies and you might be left with like four or five but yes, a true fae can be killed, so swears the summer court.<br /> <br /> 2- not specifically raped but even when a true fae is trying to be nice they almost always get it wrong and usually has some cruel twist. Many were kept as favored pets or treasured objects, so even if the changeling's durance was not physically painful, something happened to them in Arcadia that made them not human any more. they lost that in the hedge. so even if the changeling has no personal grudge against their keeper, they still have to deal with the fact that they go home to their wives as a sentient puddle or their now so beautiful and charming that they can't relate to people anymore on any real level. please note that these are the lucky ones. many are abused in one form or another and many many more never make it home at all.<br /> <br /> 3- not at all! changelings and mages usually get along very well at first, after all what is a changeling but irrefutable proof that magic still has a connection to the material world? and its always nice to have a friend who can turn your enemies in lawn furniture. of course once Arcadia gets named dropped, this changes. Mages connect their souls to magical realms of existence that connects them to their magic, one is known as Arcadia, the abode of the fae. so when a mage meets someone who's actually physically been there, well they want to know more or even worse go there themselves. Mages are humans with supernaturally enhanced will, so taking &quot;no not in a million years your scaring me please leave me alone&quot; for an answer is not always a guarente. Changelings are survivors of a place where you couldn't even trust the berries on the bush or the water in your cup. so trusting that the mage has her best interest at heart is...difficult at the best of times. a planned (possibly forced) excusrion back to Arcadia is kind of a deal breaker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}